# The first rule written for Polish rather than lifted for Italian: the locus
# of the alveolo-palatals, the series Polish has and Italian has not.
#
# What it says is what a value rule says: the formant targets a consonant is
# spoken with, each one twice because the transition into it and the one out of
# it are separate numbers. The names come from lang/plpl/plpl.globals, which is
# where what we have worked the language out to mean is written down.
#
# The numbers are a starting point and not an answer. Polish ś and ź sit
# between Italian's palatal, whose second formant is 1800, and its dentals at
# 1700, with a third formant higher than either because the tongue is further
# forward: 2000 and 2700 is the first guess, and the ear settles it.

rule pol_alveolopalatal_Fv takes 1 from is_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set f1_in to 300
  set f1_out to 300
  set f2_in to 2000
  set f2_out to 2000
  set f3_in to 2700
  set f3_out to 2700
  set f4_in to 3500
  set f4_out to 3500
  match
end
